DAY 23 — WIRESHARK (QUICK NOTES)

Wireshark = packet capture + network traffic analysis.

CORE FILTERS
dns → DNS traffic
http → HTTP traffic
tls → TLS/HTTPS traffic
tcp → TCP traffic
udp → UDP traffic
ip.addr == X.X.X.X → traffic involving an IP
tcp.port == 80 → TCP port 80

TCP HANDSHAKE
SYN → SYN-ACK → ACK

HTTP vs HTTPS
HTTP → application data can be readable.
HTTPS → HTTP data is protected by TLS encryption.

TCP STREAM
Right-click packet → Follow → TCP Stream
→ Reconstructs the conversation between client and server.

BASIC WORKFLOW
Capture → Filter → Identify protocol → Inspect packets → Follow conversation.

PRACTICAL USE
Wireshark helps understand:

DNS lookups
TCP connections
HTTP requests
TLS connections
Network communication patterns

IMPORTANT
Only capture/analyze traffic you are authorized to inspect.
